{'gap_id': 'GAP-044', 'category': 'SW', 'priority': 'P2', 'status': 'OPEN', 'skill': 'governance', 'section': None, 'description': "A KNOWN-WRONG AUTHOR ROW THAT NO SANCTIONED WRITER CAN CORRECT. REF-01002's fourth author is stored as 'Weiner, Jerome M.' (from TRID, a record GAP-026 already showed wrong on its publisher field). The publisher's own table of contents for J Architectural and Planning Research 26(2), Summer 2009 -- lockescience.com/TOC262.pdf, persisted in the batch-20 retrieval log as 07da0016d338f0f8.pdf, a born-digital text PDF (no page images; embedded Times New Roman), rendered and read -- prints 'Jerome M. Welner'. THE ROW CANNOT BE FIXED: correct-source REFUSES DOI-less sources ('no DOI, so no payload can be keyed to it'), its payload map reads only Crossref-shaped JSON, and it is the only verb that rewrites an admitted source's author rows (add-source writes them once, at admission); CLAUDE.md section 4 forbids hand SQL on a table the CLI should reach. That is a coverage bug, not a licence to bypass. WHY IT MATTERS MORE THAN ONE LETTER: the corpus's signature failure (2026-08-19) was a wrong author list that six gates passed; here the right name is in hand, persisted and rendered, and the wrong one stays because the correction path only trusts DOI-keyed payloads. Grey and pre-DOI sources -- REF-01005, REF-01008, every T5/T6 row -- have the same exposure. WHAT WOULD CLOSE IT: let correct-source take a persisted non-Crossref artefact (a publisher TOC, a title page render) with an explicit field map and its own verify-authors comparison, then correct REF-01002 through it. Derive the row's state rather than trusting this text: select position, last_name, first_name from evidence_source_authors where ref_id='REF-01002'.", 'created_at': '2026-09-25 05:02', 'created_by_session': 'session_2026-09-25-research-batch-20-audit-cluster-templer-fhwa', 'updated_at': '2026-09-25 05:02', 'updated_by_session': 'session_2026-09-25-research-batch-20-audit-cluster-templer-fhwa', 'falsification_condition': None, 'confidence_interval': None, 'shift_conditions': None, 'named_dissenter': None, 'mining_addressability': None}

